	I too have tried messing with the color palette with no changes.
I even tried setting everything to black (000).

	Some other things I have noticed -- not necessarily Mac Nethack
bugs, but:

	Occasionally when you read a scroll or quaff an unknown potion that
is supposed to say something like "the scroll disintegrates as you pick it up",
then you are asked to name it, the message that asks you to name it seems to
"cover" up the message about what happened.  What you see on the screen is
something like:

What do you want to drink? [ghj or ?*]h
Call a purple potion?

Then once you type in a name (like: xxx), those two lines in the message
window now say:

What do you want to drink? [ghj or ?*]h
This tastes like fruit juice!!
Call a purple potion?xxx


	Another thing that I often have trouble with (which I had trouble with
on an Indigo with NH 3.1.2) is that when you are presented with a single
item (i.e. quaffing with only one potion in you inventory), when I try to
get a listing of the item with the "?" option (in response to a line like the
first one in the examples above), it simply restates the question over again
without telling me what the item is.

	Something similar that has been happening tonight, is when I ask it
to list what an item is, it lists the correct item letter followed by the
description of a completely different object!

	With putting items in boxes and bags, the "#" option does not seem
to work, when I try to put 6 out of my 8 food rations in the bag, it puts
all of them in.

	The message window has a tendency to pop up infront of the dungeon
map.  With the default window location (top window bar of message window
placed underneath the bottom edge of the dungeon map) this means that the
bottom line of the stats gets obscured.  Moving the window gets around this
of course....

	Messages in the message window often scroll beneath the bottom of the
message window (or the last line is obscured by something -- the line for
the buttons??).

	Screen drawing/redrawing is very slow (using a IIci w System 7 (there's
the problem!!) with 2M memory allocated for nethack).  This is mainly when
switching from dungeon level to dungeon level and back and forth from
outside monster to inside monster (just try doing it 10 or 20 times in a row...
it's just not fun with it this slow!!! 8^}.


